Can-fail proof for SC1 layer (b) -- user election.

Setup: cloud.blonie.PasskeyVault.AutoFill was explicitly ignored via
`xcrun simctl spawn <udid> pluginkit -e ignore -i cloud.blonie.PasskeyVault.AutoFill`,
then re-queried with `pluginkit -mAvv -i cloud.blonie.PasskeyVault.AutoFill` (the same query
layer-b performs, run manually here so the election verb is NOT re-issued before the check).

Raw pluginkit output (leading marker is `-`, meaning "explicitly ignored", not `+`):

-    cloud.blonie.PasskeyVault.AutoFill(1.0)
            Path = .../PasskeyVault.app/PlugIns/PasskeyVaultAutoFill.appex
            UUID = 448F4DA4-9301-43EC-B4B3-597AF7676208
            Timestamp = 2026-08-11 2:00:45 PM +0000
            SDK = com.apple.authentication-services-credential-provider-ui
            Parent Bundle = .../PasskeyVault.app
            Display Name = Passkey Vault AutoFill
            Short Name = Passkey Vault AutoFill
            Parent Name = PasskeyVault

 (1 plug-in)

Assertion applied: grep -qE '^\+[[:space:]]*cloud.blonie.PasskeyVault.AutoFill' <output>
Result: no match. grep exit code: 1.

This demonstrates layer-b's assertion is not vacuous: with the bundle explicitly ignored
(not elected), the same positive-election pattern the PASS path requires does not match.

Restoration: scripts/ios-autofill-layers.sh layer-b was re-run immediately afterward, which
reissued `pluginkit -e use` and confirmed the elected state again (outcome=PASS, see
ios/evidence/36/pluginkit-elected.txt, which reflects the restored/final state).
